<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 31 July, from 1492 to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1492</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deadline passes for Jews to leave Spain under the Alhambra Decree</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The last day allowed by Ferdinand and Isabella's expulsion edict passed, and Spain's Jewish communities left or converted. Tens of thousands went into exile, founding the Sephardic diaspora.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1556</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ignatius of Loyola dies in Rome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ignatius of Loyola, the Basque soldier turned founder of the Society of Jesus, died in Rome. His Spiritual Exercises and the Jesuits' schools and missions reshaped Catholicism worldwide.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1703</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Daniel Defoe stands in the pillory for seditious libel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Daniel Defoe began three days in the pillory for a satirical pamphlet mocking Tory hostility to Dissenters. By tradition the crowd threw flowers instead of filth. He later wrote Robinson Crusoe.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1790</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first US patent is issued to Samuel Hopkins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Hopkins received the first patent under the new US Patent Act, for an improved way of making potash. It was signed by George Washington and Thomas Jefferson.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1917</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Passchendaele begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French forces opened the Third Battle of Ypres in Flanders. Heavy rain turned the battlefield into a swamp, and months of fighting won a few miles for hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1971</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 15 astronauts drive the first rover on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">David Scott and James Irwin took the battery-powered Lunar Roving Vehicle on its first drive near Hadley Rille. The rover let astronauts range much farther from their lander to collect samples.</p></li></ol>
